I found the bug! `head_dim=256` is passed to `tria_kv_compress`, but the stats have `head_dim=64`! The Qwen3.6-27B model has `head_dim=256` (n_embd / n_head = 6144 / 24 = 256), but the stats are for Qwen3.5-27B which has `head_dim=64` (4096 / 64 = 64).

This is a stats/model mismatch. The stats file needs to be for Qwen3.6-27B with `head_dim=256`, not Qwen3.5-27B. Or the code needs to handle this mismatch properly.

The crash happens because the code allocates `k_bf16` with size `head_dim * seq_len * n_head_kv = 256 * 65 * 4 = 66560` elements, but the tria_k_pre_rope buffer has size `head_dim * max_ctx * n_head_kv = 64 * 4096 * 4 = 1048576` elements (as shown by the ne=[256,4096,4] which is actually stored as [head_dim/2, max_ctx, n_head_kv] based on the stride calculation).

